=== reading these numbers ===
Single-threaded, one size class, one run, one machine.  They are the right
order of magnitude for "what does this mode cost me", and they are NOT a
substitute for measuring your own workload.  No aarch64 measurement.

Two results need explaining rather than quoting:

  contents  -> 1.01x (no measurable cost)
  firewall  -> 1.01x (no measurable cost)

Neither means the mode is free.  `contents` records buffer contents into the
content log and is only meaningful together with audit (the mode's own
documentation says "with audit"); alone, it does not engage on this path.
`firewall` places a guard page per allocation only at or above
umem_minfirewall, and this benchmark allocates 64 bytes, which is below the
default threshold -- so the mode is on but never triggers.  A firewall
measurement at a size that actually crosses the threshold would be much
more expensive (one page plus one unmapped page per allocation).

These two rows are therefore evidence that the BENCHMARK does not exercise
those modes, not evidence that the modes are cheap.  That is why the
documentation now carries the measured audit/guards/lite figures and says
plainly that contents and firewall are unmeasured.
